    <string name="safety_first_aid">First Aid</string>
    <string name="safety_first_aid_desc">Basic medical assistance</string>
    <string name="safety_before_content">General preparation guidelines: Keep an emergency kit ready, know your evacuation routes, and stay informed.</string>
    <string name="safety_during_content">General survival guidelines: Stay calm, follow official instructions, and use PRANSETU SOS if in immediate danger.</string>
    <string name="safety_after_content">General recovery guidelines: Wait for official clearance before returning home, check for injuries, and report damage.</string>
    <string name="safety_first_aid_content">Basic first aid: Apply pressure to bleeding wounds, keep injured persons still, and do not move people with suspected spinal injuries unless in immediate danger.</string>

    <!-- Safety Detail Content (Cyclone) -->
    <string name="safety_cyclone_before_title">Before a Cyclone</string>
    <string name="safety_cyclone_before_content">• Keep an emergency kit ready with water, food, medicines, flashlight, and batteries.\n• Know your nearest cyclone shelter.\n• Secure loose objects around your house.\n• Store important documents in waterproof bags.\n• Charge all mobile devices fully.\n• Keep PRANSETU installed and mesh mode enabled.</string>
    <string name="safety_cyclone_during_title">During a Cyclone</string>
    <string name="safety_cyclone_during_content">• Stay indoors away from windows.\n• Move to a cyclone shelter if instructed.\n• Do not go outside during the eye of the cyclone.\n• Use PRANSETU SOS if you need emergency help.\n• Listen to official announcements.\n• Stay away from flooded roads and fallen power lines.</string>
    <string name="safety_cyclone_after_title">After a Cyclone</string>
    <string name="safety_cyclone_after_content">• Do not touch downed power lines.\n• Avoid walking through flood water.\n• Check on neighbours and elderly people.\n• Report damage through PRANSETU.\n• Drink only boiled or purified water.\n• Wait for official clearance before returning home.</string>

    <!-- Safety Detail Content (Flood) -->
    <string name="safety_flood_before_title">Before a Flood</string>
    <string name="safety_flood_before_content">• Know your area\'s flood risk and evacuation routes.\n• Keep an emergency kit with essentials.\n• Move valuables to higher ground.\n• Ensure proper drainage around your home.\n• Store drinking water in clean containers.\n• Keep PRANSETU ready for emergency communication.</string>
    <string name="safety_flood_during_title">During a Flood</string>
    <string name="safety_flood_during_content">• Move to higher ground immediately.\n• Do not walk, swim, or drive through flood waters.\n• Avoid bridges over fast-moving water.\n• Use PRANSETU SOS if you are trapped.\n• Stay away from electrical equipment.\n• Follow evacuation orders promptly.</string>
    <string name="safety_flood_after_title">After a Flood</string>
    <string name="safety_flood_after_content">• Return home only when authorities say it is safe.\n• Clean and disinfect everything that got wet.\n• Check for structural damage before entering buildings.\n• Throw away food that has been in contact with flood water.\n• Watch for snakes and insects.\n• Report damage and seek assistance through PRANSETU.</string>

    <!-- Safety Detail Content (Earthquake) -->
    <string name="safety_earthquake_before_title">Before an Earthquake</string>
    <string name="safety_earthquake_before_content">• Identify safe spots in each room (under sturdy furniture).\n• Practice Drop, Cover, and Hold On.\n• Secure heavy furniture to walls.\n• Keep an emergency kit ready.\n• Know how to turn off gas, water, and electricity.\n• Keep PRANSETU installed for emergency communication.</string>
    <string name="safety_earthquake_during_title">During an Earthquake</string>
    <string name="safety_earthquake_during_content">• DROP to your hands and knees.\n• Take COVER under a sturdy desk or table.\n• HOLD ON until shaking stops.\n• If outdoors, move away from buildings and power lines.\n• If driving, stop safely and stay in the vehicle.\n• Use PRANSETU SOS if you are trapped or injured.</string>
    <string name="safety_earthquake_after_title">After an Earthquake</string>
    <string name="safety_earthquake_after_content">• Check yourself and others for injuries.\n• Expect aftershocks — be prepared to Drop, Cover, Hold On again.\n• Check for gas leaks and structural damage.\n• Do not enter damaged buildings.\n• Use PRANSETU to report your status and request help.\n• Listen for official updates.</string>

